  "chapter": {
    "number": 26,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(27) A Psalm of David, before he was anointed."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is my light and my Saviour; whom shall I fear? the Lord is the defender of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When evil-doers drew near against me to eat up my flesh, my persecutors and my enemies, they fainted and fell.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Though an army should set itself in array against me, my heart shall not be afraid: though war should rise up against me, in this am I confident.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "One thing have I asked of the Lord, this will I earnestly seek: that I should dwell in the house of the Lord, all the days of my life, that I should behold the fair beauty of the Lord, and survey his temple.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For in the day of my afflictions he hid me in his tabernacle: he sheltered me in the secret of his tabernacle; he set me up on a rock.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And now, behold, he has lifted up my head over my enemies: I went round and offered in his tabernacle the sacrifice of",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 47
          },
          {
            "text": "joy; I will sing",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 48
          },
          {
            "text": "even sing psalms to the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear, O Lord, my voice which I have uttered aloud: pity me, and listen to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My heart said to you, I have diligently sought your face: your face, O Lord, I will seek.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn not your face away from me, turn not you away from your servant in anger: be you my helper, forsake me not; and, O God my Saviour, overlook me not.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my father and my mother have forsaken me, but the Lord has taken me to himself.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Teach me, O Lord, in your way, and guide me in a right path, because of my enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me not over to the desire of them that afflict me; for unjust witnesses have risen up against me, and injustice has lied within herself.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I believe that I shall see the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 49
          },
          {
            "text": "goodness of the Lord in the land of the living.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Wait on the Lord: be of good courage, and let your heart be strengthened: yes wait on the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 47,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. shouting.",
        "reference": {
